.TH TIK 1 "2026-06-02" "tik 0.1.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tik \- count BPE tokens in text files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tik
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ FILE... ]
.br
.B tik generate-completion
.I SHELL
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tik
counts BPE tokens in text files or standard input.
When no files are provided, input is read from standard input.
For a single file or standard input, only the token count is printed.
For multiple files, each line contains the file name and token count,
separated by a tab.
.PP
Binary files are silently skipped in multi-file mode.
A binary file supplied by itself is an error.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Encoding Selection
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-encoding " " \fINAME\fR
BPE encoding name, such as
.BR cl100k_base " or " o200k_base .
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-model " " \fINAME\fR
Model name that resolves to an encoding, such as
.BR gpt-4o " or " llama-3.1-70b .
The
.B \-e
and
.B \-m
options are mutually exclusive.
.TP
.B \-\-list-encodings
Print available encoding names and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list-models
Print recognized model-prefix to encoding mappings and exit.
.SS Output
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output a JSON array instead of plain text.
Each entry contains a
.B file
field and a
.B token_count
field.
For standard input,
.B file
is
.BR null .
.SS Shell Completion
.TP
.BR generate-completion " " \fISHELL\fR
Generate a completion script for
.BR bash ", " zsh ", " fish ", " elvish ", or " powershell .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TIK_ENCODING
Default BPE encoding, overridden by
.BR \-e " or " \-\-encoding .
.TP
.B TIK_MODEL
Default model, overridden by
.BR \-m " or " \-\-model .
.PP
Flag values take precedence over environment variables.
The built-in default encoding is
.BR cl100k_base .
.SH EXAMPLES
Count tokens in one file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
tik README.md
.fi
.RE
.PP
Count tokens in multiple files:
.PP
.RS
.nf
tik src/*.rs
.fi
.RE
.PP
Read from standard input:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cat prompt.txt | tik
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use a model-specific encoding:
.PP
.RS
.nf
tik --model gpt-4o src/main.rs
.fi
.RE
.PP
Produce machine-readable output:
.PP
.RS
.nf
tik --json src/*.rs | jq
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The input was processed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
An invalid option, encoding, model, input, or file was encountered.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR jq (1)
.SH AUTHORS
graelo <https://github.com/graelo/tik>
